        190.4170379638672,
        459.5862121582031,
        198.5031280517578
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For the base model, we use the widely adopted open-source evaluation framework lm-evaluation-",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        224.9793701171875,
        505.6537780761719,
        233.88592529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "harness [125], except for the HumanEval-FIM metric, which is not supported by the framework.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        235.88836669921875,
        505.7450866699219,
        244.794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For HumanEval-FIM on the base model and all evaluation metrics on the instruct model, we use an",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        246.79833984375,
        504.002685546875,
        255.70489501953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "internal evaluation library. We choose the internal library as lm-evaluation-harness shows greater",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        257.70733642578125,
        504.1702880859375,
        266.6138916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "deviation from the LLaMA3 results reported by Yang et al. [25], relative to our internal evaluation.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        268.6163330078125,
        501.5226135253906,
        277.52288818359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For benchmarks evaluated via conditional likelihood estimation, we use Monte Carlo estimation to",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        285.0043640136719,
        503.9976806640625,
        293.9109191894531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approximate Eq. (6) for LLaDA. Since MMLU, CMMLU, and C-EVAL only require the likelihood",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        295.9133605957031,
        504.0002136230469,
        304.8199157714844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of a single token, a single Monte Carlo estimate is sufficient for these benchmarks. For all other",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        306.8223571777344,
        504.1701354980469,
        315.7289123535156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "benchmarks, we find that 128 Monte Carlo samples are adequate to produce stable results.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        317.7313537597656,
        467.4206848144531,
        326.6379089355469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For benchmarks evaluated using conditional generation, we apply pure diffusion sampling with a",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        334.120361328125,
        503.9974060058594,
        343.02691650390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "low-confidence remasking strategy to both LLaDA Base and LLaDA Instruct. For LLaDA Base, we",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        345.02935791015625,
        504.004150390625,
        353.9359130859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "set both the generation length and the number of sampling steps to 1024. For LLaDA Instruct, the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        355.9383544921875,
        504.00164794921875,
        364.84490966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "number of sampling steps is set equal to the answer length, which is configured as follows: 3 for",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        366.84735107421875,
        504.1700439453125,
        375.75390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MMLU and HellaSwag, 64 for GPQA, 256 for MBPP and MMLU-Pro, and 512 for HumanEval,",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        377.75634765625,
        505.2474060058594,
        386.66290283203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "GSM8K, Math, and ARC-C. As detailed in Appendix B.4, for HumanEval, MBPP, GSM8K, Math,",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        388.6653747558594,
        505.24700927734375,
        397.5719299316406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and GPQA, we set the confidence of the |EOS| token to zero during sampling for LLaDA Instruct.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        398.8580322265625,
        499.3009338378906,
        408.4819030761719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "B.7",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        429.14178466796875,
        122.11700439453125,
        438.0981750488281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Analysis of Sampling Efficiency",
      "bbox": [
        132.07960510253906,
        429.14178466796875,
        266.3156433105469,
        438.0981750488281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this section, we first analyze the sampling efficiency of LLaDA, including both sampling speed",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        451.3273620605469,
        503.99517822265625,
        460.2339172363281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and memory consumption. We then discuss potential optimizations to further improve its efficiency.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        462.2363586425781,
        505.66796875,
        471.1429138183594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We use four representative open-ended generation benchmarks for sampling speed analysis: GSM8K,",
      "bbox": [
        107.53199768066406,
        478.6253662109375,
        505.2473449707031,
        487.53192138671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Math, HumanEval, and MBPP. We use the widely adopted throughput metric to measure generation",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        489.53436279296875,
        503.9967041015625,
        498.44091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "speed, defined as the number of tokens generated per second. We compare LLaDA 8B Base and",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        500.443359375,
        503.9974670410156,
        509.34991455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LLaMA3 8B Base, both using bfloat16 precision. All experiments in this section were conducted on",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        511.35235595703125,
        503.998291015625,
        520.2589111328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a single A100-80GB GPU with a batch size of 1. For LLaDA, the output length is fixed to 256 tokens",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        522.2613525390625,
        504.00164794921875,
        531.1679077148438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "across all four benchmarks.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        533.1703491210938,
        217.5587158203125,
        542.076904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fig. 5 shows that LLaDA enables a flexible trade-off between generation quality and speed by",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        549.559326171875,
        504.34283447265625,
        558.4658813476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "adjusting the number of sampling steps. Specifically, on the GSM8K and Math datasets, LLaDA",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        560.4683837890625,
        504.3529357910156,
        569.3749389648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "8B Base achieves comparable performance to LLaMA3 8B Base while delivering 1.5 and 1.8 times",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        571.3773803710938,
        504.0034484863281,
        580.283935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "higher throughput, even though LLaMA3 uses KV Cache and LLaDA operates without any inference",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        582.286376953125,
        504.0013427734375,
        591.1929321289062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "optimization techniques. For the HumanEval benchmark, LLaDA 8B Base performs comparably to",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        593.1953735351562,
        504.0003967285156,
        602.1019287109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LLaMA3 8B Base when the throughput is matched. On the MBPP benchmark, LLaDA 8B Base lags",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        604.1043701171875,
        503.99932861328125,
        613.0109252929688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "behind LLaMA3 8B Base.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        615.0133666992188,
        213.70314025878906,
        623.919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For LLaMA3, the acceleration benefit provided by KV caching is notably weaker on the HumanEval",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        631.40234375,
        504.0005798339844,
        640.3088989257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dataset, which can be attributed to its relatively short prompt lengths. Specifically, the average prompt",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        642.3113403320312,
        504.0014953613281,
        651.2178955078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lengths for GSM8K, Math, MBPP, and HumanEval are 894, 680, 628, and 132 tokens, respectively.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        653.2203369140625,
        504.5213928222656,
        662.1268920898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tab. 11 compares of memory consumption between LLaDA 8B Base and LLaMA3 8B Base. To",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        669.609375,
        504.0032653808594,
        678.5159301757812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "avoid variations in generation length caused by differences in training data, we fix both the input",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        680.5183715820312,
        503.9972839355469,
        689.4249267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and output token lengths during the memory analysis. For LLaDA, memory usage remains constant",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        691.4273681640625,
        503.9975280761719,
        700.3339233398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "regardless of the number of sampling steps. Its memory consumption is comparable to LLaMA3 8B",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        702.3363647460938,
        504.0013427734375,
        711.242919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Base without KV cache, but slightly higher than with KV cache.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        713.245361328125,
        364.5767517089844,
        722.1519165039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "27",
      "bbox": [
